    <innerclass refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1Helper" prot="public">api::v2::Helper</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi">api</innernamespace>
    <innernamespace refid="namespaceapi_1_1v2">api::v2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Factory for the standard JSON HTTP responses used by the v2 controllers and filters. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header declares the <ref refid="helper_8cpp_1a5993cee5fba70417c6e9bb08de6b2016" kindref="member">Helper</ref> utility class. Its static functions build the three kinds of reply the API sends: a 500 &quot;Failure&quot;, an arbitrary-status &quot;Error&quot;, and a 200 &quot;Success&quot; whose body is already JSON. A private reply function does the actual work of setting the status, content type and body, and adds a Retry-After header to 503 replies. The prepare function wraps a message in a JSON object with a &quot;Status&quot; field.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: <ref refid="helper_8cpp_1a5993cee5fba70417c6e9bb08de6b2016" kindref="member">Helper</ref> gives the entire API one consistent response format. Controllers and filters call these functions instead of hand-building HTTP responses, so clients always receive the same JSON shape for errors and the same headers for retryable failures. It is used by <ref refid="common_8hpp" kindref="compound">common.hpp</ref>, the Auth filter and every route controller. Without it each handler would invent its own error format and clients could not reliably understand failures.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Static utility class: a class used as a namespace for functions, never instantiated.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP status codes: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::function callback: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/functional/function</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>JSON: <ulink url="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/JSON</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
